Ruby vs JavaScript:
    
    1. Ruby Example
       class User
           attr_accessor :name, :age
           
           def initialize(name, age)
               @name = name
               @age = age
           end
           
           def greet
               \"Hello, I'm #{@name}\"
           end
       end
        
       user = User.new('John', 30)
       puts user.greet
    
    2. JavaScript Example
       class User {
           constructor(name, age) {
               this.name = name;
               this.age = age;
           }
           
           greet() {
               return `Hello, I'm ${this.name}`;
           }
       }
        
       const user = new User('John', 30);
       console.log(user.greet());
    
    3. Comparison Table
       Feature | Ruby | JavaScript
       --------|------|-----------
       Paradigm | OOP | Prototype
       Syntax | Elegant | C-like
       Server | Yes | Yes (Node.js)
       Client | No | Yes
       Concurrency | Threads | Event loop
       Framework | Rails | React/Vue
       Typing | Dynamic | Dynamic
       Learning | Moderate | Moderate
    
    4. When to Choose
       Ruby | JavaScript
       ----|-----------
       Backend APIs | Frontend
       Rails development | Web development
       Server-side | Client-side
       Elegant code | Universal
       Full-stack | Interactive UIs

