Ruby and Java are both object-oriented languages with different design goals. In 2026: 1) Ruby - dynamic, interpreted, 2) Java - static, compiled, 3) Ruby - elegant syntax, 4) Java - verbose syntax, 5) Ruby - dynamic typing, 6) Java - static typing, 7) Ruby - Rails, 8) Java - Spring, 9) Ruby - faster development, 10) Java - better performance. Choose Ruby for rapid development, Java for performance and enterprise.

Example:
```ruby
Ruby vs Java:
    
    1. Ruby Example
       class User
           attr_accessor :name, :age
           
           def initialize(name, age)
               @name = name
               @age = age
           end
           
           def greet
               \"Hello, I'm #{@name}\"
           end
       end
        
       user = User.new('John', 30)
       puts user.greet
    
    2. Java Example
       public class User {
           private String name;
           private int age;
           
           public User(String name, int age) {
               this.name = name;
               this.age = age;
           }
           
           public String getName() {
               return name;
           }
           
           public int getAge() {
               return age;
           }
           
           public String greet() {
               return \"Hello, I'm \" + name;
           }
       }
        
       public class Main {
           public static void main(String[] args) {
               User user = new User(\"John\", 30);
               System.out.println(user.greet());
           }
       }
    
    3. Comparison Table
       Feature | Ruby | Java
       --------|------|-------
       Typing | Dynamic | Static
       Execution | Interpreted | Compiled
       Syntax | Elegant | Verbose
       Framework | Rails | Spring
       Performance | Slower | Faster
       Enterprise | Limited | Excellent
       Learning | Easier | Harder
       Use Case | Startups | Enterprise
    
    4. When to Choose
       Ruby | Java
       ----|--------
       Rapid development | Enterprise
       Startups | Large companies
       Rails | Spring
       Elegant code | Type safety
       MVP | Long-term projects
```

Detailed Explanation:
Ruby is dynamic with elegant syntax for rapid development (Rails). Java is static with verbose syntax for enterprise and performance (Spring). Choose Ruby for speed, Java for enterprise.

